```
$ ling --help
Search, inspect, tokenize, and prepare Japanese corpora

Usage: ling [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  matches         Find lingrep patterns matches and stream one record per match
  summarize       Aggregate matches per pattern into exact group counts
  tokenize        Tokenize a corpus and stream sentence and token records
  coverage        Report attribute coverage, and which catalog exclusions absence exposes
  explore         Browse matches interactively in the terminal
  sentence-final  Aggregate matches selected by sentence-final policy
  corpus          Build or inspect artifacts, or inventory corpus sources
  check           Compile and validate an lingrep patterns catalog without reading a corpus
  doctor          Probe dictionary, catalog, and prepared-corpus inputs
  describe        Describe command arguments, examples, and owned contracts
  contracts       List or describe stable machine-output contracts
  completions     Generate a shell completion definition
  manpages        Generate manual pages for every public command
  help            Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Output:
      --json           Write JSONL records and machine-readable JSON diagnostics
      --color <COLOR>  Control ANSI styling in human output [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]

lingrep patterns syntax: run `ling check --help` or read ling-check(1).

```
